      "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1\\times 4}{6} = \\dfrac{4}{6}\n$$\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we can divide the numerator and denominator by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4\\div 2}{6\\div 2} = \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$",
